            "findingId/v1": "T-4"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "6.7",
            "control-status": "missing",
            "control-evidence": [],
            "control-carry-forward": false,
            "control-effectiveness": "none",
            "maestro-layer": "L6 \u2014 Security and Compliance",
            "inherent-risk": "6.7",
            "residual-risk": "6.7",
            "recommendation": "Implement input validation for auth-broker. Validate each structured input against a closed schema before use, and reject unknown fields and oversized values. Place the control where credential assertions and session grants are first received, so that nothing downstream has to repeat the check. This addresses: Unsanitised credential assertions and session grants reach auth-broker and are processed as trusted structure, so crafted input changes how later steps interpret the record. Acceptance check: malformed, oversized and unexpected fields are rejected before any side effect, and a regression test covers each rejected shape. Roll the change out behind a flag, watch error rates for one release and remove the flag once no regression is seen. Suggested location: stub-codebase/src/auth_broker/input_validation.py. Reference patterns: Schema validation, parameterised queries, output encoding.",
            "effort-estimate": "Medium"
          }
        },
