            "recommendation": "Implement input validation for worker-2. Validate each structured input against a closed schema before use, and reject unknown fields and oversized values. Place the control where work orders and route candidates are first received, so that nothing downstream has to repeat the check. This addresses: Markdown or HTML produced by worker-2 contains remote images that leak data when a client renders it. Acceptance check: malformed, oversized and unexpected fields are rejected before any side effect, and a regression test covers each rejected shape. Apply the change to the most exposed instances first, then to the rest, and keep the previous configuration available for a quick rollback. Suggested location: stub-codebase/src/worker_2/input_validation.py. Reference patterns: Schema validation, parameterised queries, output encoding.",
