            "inherent-risk": "7.9",
            "residual-risk": "5.9",
            "recommendation": "Harden the existing access control control: evaluate the original caller's entitlement for each object and action, and deny by default when the check cannot be made on the paths of auth-broker that it does not yet cover. The current implementation is recorded at src/gateway/token_verify.py:7 and covers the main request path. Extend it to the secondary paths and add a test that exercises each of them. This addresses: A shared or long-lived refresh token on auth-broker lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. Acceptance check: a caller without the entitlement is denied for every object and action, including through indirect paths, and the denial is recorded. Ship to the internal environment first, compare behaviour with the previous release and promote after reviewing the first week of records. Suggested location: src/gateway/token_verify.py. Reference patterns: Role and attribute checks at the service boundary, deny-by-default policy.",
            "effort-estimate": "Medium"
          }
