            "recommendation": "Implement encryption for vector-store-a. Protect this data in transit and at rest with current protocols and keys held outside the storage account. Place the control where embedded documents and metadata are first received, so that nothing downstream has to repeat the check. This addresses: embedded documents and metadata held by vector-store-a are readable by any service in the Data Zone that shares the same network role, because access is granted by network position. Acceptance check: a scan of the link or store shows only current protocol versions and encrypted content, and keys rotate without downtime. Apply the change to the most exposed instances first, then to the rest, and keep the previous configuration available for a quick rollback. Suggested location: stub-codebase/src/vector_store_a/encryption.py. Reference patterns: TLS 1.3, envelope encryption, managed key service.",
