            "recommendation": "Harden the existing logging/audit control: record who did what, to which object, with which outcome, in a store that operators cannot alter on the paths of tool-server-1 that it does not yet cover. The current implementation is recorded at src/audit/ledger_writer.py:9 and covers the main request path. Extend it to the secondary paths and add a test that exercises each of them. This addresses: Actions taken through tool-server-1 are logged without the authenticated principal or a request identifier, so a caller can deny having submitted a change to tool call arguments and results. Acceptance check: every state change produces one complete record that an operator cannot edit, and a gap in the sequence raises an alert. Ship to the internal environment first, compare behaviour with the previous release and promote after reviewing the first week of records. Suggested location: src/audit/ledger_writer.py. Reference patterns: Append-only ledger, hash chaining, structured events.",
